OL,3,GNEWSA'Slippery leaves' to blame for
OL,4,Atrain cancellations
OL,5,
OL,6,FRail services in East Yorkshire
OL,7,Faffected by falling leaves will revert
OL,8,Fto normal "as soon as it is safe", says
OL,9,Fa train operator.
OL,11,FNorthern Rail services have seen
OL,12,Fnumerous cancellations since last
OL,13,FFriday, impacting passengers travelling
OL,14,Fbetween Hull, Driffield, Beverley and
OL,15,FCottingham.
OL,17,FA Northern spokesperson said the leaves
OL,18,Fhad compressed on the rails and formed
OL,19,F"a thin, slippery layer which can cause
OL,20,Ftrains to slide".
OL,23,APub: 04-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBYrk Lincs NewsCReg TVFWeather
FL,384,380,200,160,0,100
